# PROJECT CONTEXT — PAYMENT SYSTEM

## Local & International Payment Architecture

### 1. Payment System Overview

The platform supports two payment categories:

* 🇪🇹 Local Payment — Ethiopia
* 🌎 International Payment — Global Users

The payment system must provide a simple, clean, secure, and compact user experience.

Users select only their preferred payment provider. Internal payment routing, gateway selection, verification, fallback logic, and payment processing are handled by the backend.

---

# 2. PRICING DISPLAY PRINCIPLE

Payment amounts must **NOT** appear at the top of the shared payment popup.

The service price is displayed on the **main website / feature card** before the user reaches the payment popup.

Example:

> **PDF to Word**
> *3 ETB for high-quality conversion*

The international pricing/access information is also displayed on the main website.

When the user clicks:

> **Save to Device**

the shared payment popup appears.

The popup is primarily for **payment-provider selection**.

The popup should NOT initially display:

> 3 ETB

or

> $1

because the same popup is used by both local and international users.

---

# 3. PAYMENT POPUP — FINAL COMPACT LAYOUT

The payment popup must prioritize **horizontal layout** and compactness.

The payment options should extend **from left to right as much as reasonably possible**, rather than creating unnecessary vertical length.

The layout is:

```text
🇪🇹  [ Telebirr ] [ CBE ] [ Dashen ] [ Abyssinia ]
        Logo         Logo      Logo        Logo


🌎  [ Airtm ] [ Paddle ] [ PayPal ]
        Logo       Logo        Logo
```

### Layout Rules

* Local payment providers are arranged horizontally.
* International payment providers are arranged horizontally.
* Provider names appear with their official logos.
* The layout should remain compact.
* Do NOT unnecessarily stack the payment providers vertically.
* Do NOT create separate large cards for each provider.
* The popup should use the available horizontal space efficiently.
* The design should be responsive for mobile/Android screens while preserving the horizontal-first principle as much as reasonably possible.
* Chapa and SantimPay are not displayed to the user.
* Local and international payment options appear in the same popup.
* No "Select International Gateway" step exists.
* The popup does not initially display the payment amount.

